---
import HomeSection from "./HomeSection.astro";
import TypewriterTail from "./TypewriterTail.astro";
import BrandImage from "./BrandImage.astro";
import logo from "../assets/ojuny-logo.png";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const phrases = ["paper cut", "opaque setup", "missing app", "hidden setting", "flake"];
---

<HomeSection id="about">
  <div class="ojuny-about">
    <div class="ojuny-about-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="ojuny-eyebrow">The short version</p>
      <h2 class="ojuny-about-title">
        We can fix every <TypewriterTail phrases={phrases} />
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ojuny-about-body">
      <div class="ojuny-about-copy" data-reveal>
        <p>
        Linux desktops usually start as a pile of dotfiles, a wiki, and a prayer.
        Ojuny starts with a flake: typed options, readable modules, and a menu
        that writes real configuration.
      </p>
      <p>
        A desktop should not trade one opaque setup for another. Ojuny keeps the
        pieces upstream and readable: MangoWM and Dux Modular Shell are documented
        projects, the configuration is Nix, and the settings menu writes real
        options. There is a GUI for temporary apps and a Flatpak store patch,
        not a terminal-only ritual.
      </p>
      <p>
        When something breaks, you read the module, change the option, and
        rebuild. You do not need to ask a model to guess at your machine.
      </p>
        <p>
          Behind it all is the <a href={`${base}doctrine/`}>Ojuny Doctrine</a>:
          seven rules for a desktop you can read, rebuild, and hand to someone
          else.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="ojuny-quote" data-reveal>
      <div class="ojuny-quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</div>
      <blockquote>
        When you install ojuny, that is not my desktop. It is yours.
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="ojuny-quote-badge">
          <BrandImage
            src={logo.src}
            width={96}
            height={96}
            alt=""
            loading="lazy"
            class="ojuny-quote-logo"
          />
        </span>
        <span class="ojuny-quote-meta">
          <strong>SDG</strong>
          <small>Maintainer, Ojuny</small>
        </span>
        <a href={`${base}getting-started/what-is-ojuny/`} aria-label="Read what Ojuny is">→</a>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</HomeSection>
